# .NET build output
bin/
obj/
*.user

# IDE
.vs/
.vscode/
*.suo

# Test results
TestResults/
*.trx

# Packaging output (Velopack, installers, self-contained publish)
Releases/
publish/
dist/

# Windows shortcuts (machine-specific absolute paths)
*.lnk

# Images dropped in the repo ROOT (screenshots, references, exports): the intentional design
# assets live in Toki-ProductDesign/ and stay tracked; only stray root-level images are ignored.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.gif
/*.bmp
/*.webp

# Trial / demo / screen-recording videos: large, machine-specific, never committed
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
*.mkv
*.webm
# On-device models, recordings, and databases (live in %APPDATA%, never committed;
# these patterns are defensive in case any land in the repo tree during dev)
*.onnx
*.gguf
*.bin
*.tar.bz2
# Audio recordings, never committed
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.aac
*.flac
*.ogg
Recordings/
# Databases
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# design-sync machine state (staged scripts, build output, caches)
.ds-sync/
ds-bundle/
.design-sync/.cache/
.design-sync/learnings/
.design-sync/node_modules
design-web/node_modules/
design-web/dist/

# WPF temp project files (build artifacts, never commit)
*_wpftmp.csproj

# The demo film (Remotion). The footage and the build output are large and regenerable;
# the composition source in video/src IS worth keeping.
video/node_modules/
video/out/
video/public/raw.mp4

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Screenshots, screen recordings and render output, ANYWHERE in the tree.
# The root-only /*.png rules above miss anything dropped into a subfolder, and
# the filming workflow (docs: film the transition, do not reason about it)
# produces contact sheets and frame dumps that are large and regenerable.
Screenshot *.png
Screenshot_*.png
Recording *.mp4
WhatsApp Image *
*-sheet.png
*-contact.png
frames/
shots/
renders/
render-out/
libshot/

# Self-test PNG output (--render <dir> / --libshot <dir>) when pointed at the repo.
toki-render/
toki-shots/

# Claude Code machine-local state. The PERMISSION list and any local settings are
# per-machine and can name absolute paths; they are never shared.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.json.bak

# NOT ignored, deliberately: .claude/skills/. Those SKILL.md files are part of the
# constitution (CLAUDE.md requires loading motion-and-feel + apple-design-motion on
# every visual change) and are the record of decisions already paid for in bugs.
# A clone without them loses the rules, so they stay tracked.
# Provenance: the vendored ones (emil-*, apple-design-motion) each carry their own
# MIT attribution line in their SKILL.md header. This repo is PRIVATE, so that is
# provenance only. If it is ever made public, that becomes a redistribution notice
# obligation and the full MIT licence text has to ship beside them.
